+# Everyday Project Autopilot
+
+Project Autopilot has a one-command interface for normal repository tasks.
+Run it from the folder that should change:
+
+```bash
+ha "Create a concise post-interview template in POST_INTERVIEW_TEMPLATE.md"
+```
+
+`ha` is a local shortcut for `hermes autopilot`. The command automatically:
+
+1. finds the Git repository and scopes work to the current folder;
+2. creates a clean shadow of committed `HEAD` when the parent repository has unrelated changes;
+3. registers the project;
+4. creates the mission, executor, and independent verifier;
+5. dispatches and waits;
+6. creates a verified local mission commit;
+7. applies the verified patch back only when it does not overlap existing local edits.
+
+When no `--verify` command is supplied, Hermes requires a whitespace-clean, nonempty Git change in the selected scope. For stronger proof, add a deterministic check:
+
+```bash
+ha "Create POST_INTERVIEW_TEMPLATE.md" \
+  --verify 'test -s POST_INTERVIEW_TEMPLATE.md'
+```
+
+Useful options:
+
+- `--repo PATH`: operate on a different folder.
+- `--path PATH`: narrow the declared contract to a specific relative path.
+- `--verify COMMAND`: provide one or more exact proof commands.
+- `--no-apply`: keep the verified result on the mission branch without applying it to the current checkout.
+- `--json`: return machine-readable output.
+
+If verified files overlap existing local edits, Hermes does not overwrite them. It saves the verified patch under `~/.hermes/autopilot/results/<mission-id>/verified.patch` and reports the conflicting paths.
